## Recommendations

**Do these first, in order:**

1. **Tape the PRD to the wall on Day 1.** The one document that constrains every decision for 56 days. Without it, scope creep wins.
2. **Build the Verification Engine in Week 2, before the Refactoring Engine in Week 4.** This is the single most counterintuitive sequencing call in the plan and the single most important. The moat is "verified," not "deterministic." Most engineers will want to build the cool transform code first. Resist.
3. **Cut from 10 transforms to 6 the moment Week 4 slips by 2 days.** 6 transforms that work perfectly beat 10 that don't. The roadmap can absorb the rest.
4. **Run beta gauntlets in Week 7 with the founder watching live.** You will learn more in 5 hours of screen-share than 5 weeks of GitHub issues.
5. **Ship MIT-licensed and free.** Pricing comes later via Refactron Cloud (CI-as-a-service, audit reports, on-prem support). The CLI must be free forever — this is the moat against Cursor adding a "verified mode."
6. **Lead every conversation with the failure data.** NYU 40% vulnerability rate. UTSA 19.7% fabricated packages. ACM 92.45% broken Copilot tests. Stripe 33% of dev time on tech debt. Stack Overflow 62% top frustration. These five numbers are your entire pitch.

**Stage 2 (Months 2–4):** Add Java + Go via the same LanguageAdapter pattern. Build the Refactron Cloud beta — same CLI, runs in your CI, posts diffs as PR comments, charges per active repo. Target ARR by month 6: $10k MRR from 20 teams at $500/mo.

**Stage 3 (Months 5–8):** Raise seed if metrics warrant it (>$10k MRR, >50k npm downloads/week, >5k stars). Hire one senior engineer focused on adding 20 more transforms. Submit a Strange Loop or USENIX ;login: paper on the deterministic-plus-verify model — academic credibility compounds in the dev-tool market.

**Benchmarks that change the recommendations:**
- If npm downloads cross 100k/month by Month 3, accelerate hiring.
- If a clone appears in the LLM-tool market with "verified mode," double engineering on transforms (depth > breadth).
- If Evōk ships and the market splits, consider acquisition conversation rather than head-to-head burn.

