## Caveats

- **The 8-week timeline assumes a solo founder working ~60 hours/week with no other obligations.** Real life — exams, family, illness — will compress some weeks. The plan has Saturday-Sunday buffer in Weeks 1, 4, 6, 7; treat them as buffer, not extra work days.
- **Some cited statistics come from secondary reporting rather than the original studies.** The "NYU 1,692 programs, ~40% vulnerable" figure circulates widely; the original is the Pearce/Ahmad/Tan/Dolan-Gavitt/Karri "Asleep at the Keyboard?" paper (IEEE S&P 2022, arXiv:2108.09293) — verify the exact number against the paper before citing in a Series-A pitch deck. The "92.45% broken Copilot tests" figure is from the ACM AST 2024 paper by El Haji et al.; the "19.7% fabricated packages" is from Spracklen et al. (USENIX Security 2024 / arXiv 2406.10279) — confirm authors/venue before official press use.
- **The Stripe Developer Coefficient is from 2018.** It is the most-cited stat for tech debt cost but it is 8 years old. McKinsey's "Tech debt: Reclaiming tech equity" (2020) and GitClear's "Code Quality" reports (2024) offer more recent numbers — use them when audience is enterprise-savvy.
- **jscodeshift's "unmaintained at Meta" status comes from facebook/jscodeshift Issue #587 (August 2024).** The Codemod team has since taken over maintenance; the project is alive, just not at Meta. Frame this accurately in messaging — "abandoned by Meta but not dead" is true; "dead" is not.
- **Tree-sitter, LibCST, and ts-morph are all actively maintained as of 2025–2026 but none are at "1.0 forever, never breaks" stability.** Pin dependency versions and budget time for breaking changes annually.
- **The "AST-based autofix at 96–100% accuracy" Semgrep figure applies only to expressions, not statements or whole-function refactors.** Do not over-extend that data point when explaining Refactron's expected accuracy — Refactron tackles harder transforms and will have a lower theoretical ceiling. The test-gate exists precisely to catch what the transform logic cannot prove.
- **The "Evōk Labs (evok.dev) is pre-product" claim was current at task brief time.** Verify their public status the week before launch; competitive intelligence ages fast.
- **The Show HN comment thread responses cannot be pre-canned word-for-word.** HN moderators detect and downrank canned replies. Use the pre-writes as scaffolding, not scripts.
- **All future-facing metrics (Day 1 / Week 1 / Month 1 targets) are aspirational, not predictions.** They're calibrated against comparable dev-tool launches (Ruff did ~6k stars Month 1; Biome had a slower start; esbuild's launch curve is the upper bound). Refactron's curve will sit somewhere in this range — closer to the upper bound if the verification-before-write framing lands, closer to the lower bound if it's perceived as a niche refactoring tool.